      },
      "displayName": "Osman Din",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A5665ee66-7fc9-476a-ba31-3a9e2e39feee",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "It seems to me that since it's only a recommendation it shouldn't be enforced. Perhaps produce a warning when a PUT is made.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "ModeShape treats both cases as the same. That is, creating 'test/' when 'test' exists results in an exception. (This is assuming that no path manipulation, e.g., truncating, is done somewhere in the stack).",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "On a side note, the PATCH request (via FedoraLDP) does not recognize the trailing slash. DELETE works ok.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
