      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A5665ee66-7fc9-476a-ba31-3a9e2e39feee",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>It seems to me that since it's only a recommendation it shouldn't be enforced. Perhaps produce a warning when a PUT is made.</p>\n\n<p>ModeShape treats both cases as the same. That is, creating 'test/' when 'test' exists results in an exception. (This is assuming that no path manipulation, e.g., truncating, is done somewhere in the stack).</p>\n\n<p>On a side note, the PATCH request (via FedoraLDP) does not recognize the trailing slash. DELETE works ok.</p>",
     "created": "31/Mar/15 12:58 PM",
     "id": "13830",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11376/comment/13830",
